        <h3>AI Search Visibility (GEO / AEO)</h3>
        <p>Entity frameworks built from Google's query fan-out patent and Koray Tuğberk's semantic model, so content is structured the way retrieval systems select and quote it. Grounded versus non-grounded citation experiments that track explicit citations and implicit brand mentions separately, because they move independently. Free tools built as LLM entry points, answers placed where models read (Reddit, Quora, G2), and LLM referral traffic segmented in GA4 so the result is measured, not assumed.</p>
        <p>The method is public: <a href="/blog/get-cited-by-ai-search/">the retrieval-readiness checklist</a>, <a href="/blog/geo-aeo-vs-seo/">how SEO, AEO and GEO sequence</a>, and <a href="/blog/breaking-my-own-study/">the study I tried to break</a>.</p>
